  "articleBody": "It's easy for electrical projects to get off track if coordination isn't a top priority. One of the biggest mistakes we see is when electrical plans aren't properly overlaid with other trade drawings early on. This can lead to frustrating clashes with plumbing or HVAC runs, creating costly rework. Another common slip-up is missing crucial panel or access clearances. You need space for everything to work safely and efficiently! People also frequently fail to coordinate penetrations and sleeves, which can cause headaches when walls are closed up. And trying to make late changes after materials are ordered or walls are already in place? That's a surefire way to blow your budget and timeline. When you're dealing with service upgrades, panel work, or multi-trade rough-in conflicts, a licensed, coordination-savvy electrician is absolutely essential. They understand the inspection deadlines and how to avoid issues where incorrect routing or clearance could force rework or delay you getting back into your home. HH Remodeling LLC works to prevent these kinds of mistakes by ensuring proper planning and coordination from the get-go.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}